<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 6.72 pct, M2 up 6.61 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 6.72 pct, M2 up 6.61 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 754.1 billion levs on June 6 from 706.6 billion levs a week earlier and M2 increased to 3,526.4 billion levs from 3,307.8 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 6.88 percent to 3,734.7 billion levs in the week to June 6.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,660.6 levs per dollar on June 6, 1,568.1 for May 30 and 1,467.8 for April 25.</p>
